# Bezier Curves Dev

```elixir
Mix.install(
  [
    {:curves, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "../"), env: :dev},
    {:tucan, "~> 0.6.0"},
    {:vega_lite, "~> 0.1.0"},
    {:kino_vega_lite, "~> 0.1.0"},
  ],
  config_path: :curves,
  lockfile: :curves
)
```

## Curves (Bezier) tutorial

```elixir
# And finally the one most people think of when they hear "bezier curve"; The cubic bezier.
curve = Curves.define_spline([
  # P0
  [{0, 0}],
  [{1, 0}],
  [{1, 1}],
  [{0, 1}],
  [{0, 2}],
  [{1, 2}],
], :b_spline)


curve
|> Curves.Utils.Plotting.curve_to_scatterplot(label: "Catmull-Rom", count: 1000)
|> Tucan.scatter("x", "y")
|> Tucan.color_by("label")
|> Tucan.fill_by("label")
```

```elixir
# And finally the one most people think of when they hear "bezier curve"; The cubic bezier.
curve = Curves.define_spline([
  # P0
  [{0, 0}],
  [{1, 0}],
  [{1, 1}],
  [{0, 1}],
  [{0, 2}],
  [{1, 2}],
], :catmull_rom)


curve
|> Curves.Utils.Plotting.curve_to_scatterplot(label: "Catmull-Rom", count: 1000)
